From: Gezim <gezimos@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 23:30:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 15/15] Kompakt: no QcRilAm

QcRilAm forwards in-call audio settings to Qualcomm's IQcRilAudio HAL. A
MediaTek phone has no such HAL, so the app found nothing to talk to, but it
is persistent: it ran from boot and could never be killed, holding 6 to 9 MB
for nothing.
---
 base.mk | 4 +---
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/base.mk b/base.mk
--- a/base.mk
+++ b/base.mk
@@ -242,9 +242,7 @@ PRODUCT_PACKAGES += \
 PRODUCT_PACKAGES += \
     evgrab \

-# QCOM in-call audio fix as a standalone app
-PRODUCT_PACKAGES += \
-    QcRilAm
+# Kompakt: no QcRilAm; it serves Qualcomm's in-call audio HAL, which a MediaTek phone does not have, and ran persistent for nothing.

 PRODUCT_PACKAGES += \
     slsi-booted \
